    <node id="esma sultan">
      <data key="d0">esma sultan</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Esma Sultan was an Ottoman princess, born on 21 March 1873 and died on 7 May 1899, known for being the daughter of Sultan Abdülaziz and Gevheri Kadın.&lt;SEP&gt;Esma Sultan was an Ottoman princess, born on 17 July 1778 and died on 4 June 1848. She was the daughter of Sultan Abdul Hamid I and the sister of Sultans Mustafa IV and Mahmud II. She also served as the adoptive mother of Bezmiâlem Sultan and Rahime Perestu Sultan.&lt;SEP&gt;Esma Sultan was an Ottoman princess and the wife of Küçük Hüseyin Pasha, linking her to the Ottoman dynasty.&lt;SEP&gt;Esma Sultan refers to the name shared by three daughters of three different Ottoman Sultans, indicating a historical significance and connection to the Ottoman Empire.&lt;SEP&gt;Esma Sultan is the original owner of the Esma Sultan Mansion, which is named in her honor, indicating her historical significance.&lt;SEP&gt;Esma Sultan was a daughter of Gevheri Kadın and Abdülaziz, also part of the Ottoman royal family.&lt;SEP&gt;Esma Sultan was an Ottoman princess, born on 14 March 1726 and died on 13 August 1788, known for being the daughter of Sultan Ahmed III and his consort Zeynep Kadın.</data>
      <data key="d3">8855ef7c0a862ad2716a4800e6daab9a4fc8a3fc3144bf260d69fbc7114ab5f6_chunk_0&lt;SEP&gt;ab86467d215b61cd3bcb04f178aad33bd273548437a1beb351bd76fe7575dae8_chunk_0&lt;SEP&gt;d7732993584e6052219909b3713bcfd07c3e2fe072a2d0dc3208947e7a9939a3_chunk_0&lt;SEP&gt;68c99ff83308fcbfb9f051305ffb9629a8a17b43febb01cf40603dcff15c1ca5_chunk_0&lt;SEP&gt;e45696a7ce3276d7f032ec5b2e379887045aff382c483b5bd22984c390e6c574_chunk_0&lt;SEP&gt;00abc8939d8e5e0dd3acda099aa550f155b8386dfee901c16f211d045eb300dc_chunk_0&lt;SEP&gt;aabfddd60fb33fe357ce8061fbadd36dd9b83032d9ea1817dc5bd725a9512e25_chunk_0</data>
      <data key="d4">null</data>
    </node>
    <node id="abd laziz">
      <data key="d0">abd laziz</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Abdülaziz was the Sultan of the Ottoman Empire and the father of Esma Sultan, known for his reign during the 19th century.&lt;SEP&gt;Abdülaziz was the 32nd Sultan of the Ottoman Empire, ruling from 1861 until his deposition in 1876.</data>
      <data key="d3">8855ef7c0a862ad2716a4800e6daab9a4fc8a3fc3144bf260d69fbc7114ab5f6_chunk_0&lt;SEP&gt;00abc8939d8e5e0dd3acda099aa550f155b8386dfee901c16f211d045eb300dc_chunk_0</data>
      <data key="d4">null</data>
    </node>
    <node id="gevheri kad n">
      <data key="d0">gevheri kad n</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Gevheri Kadın was the wife of Sultan Abdülaziz and the mother of Esma Sultan, contributing to the royal lineage of the Ottoman Empire.&lt;SEP&gt;Gevheri Kadın was the fifth wife of the 32nd Ottoman Sultan Abdülaziz and the mother of Şehzade Mehmed Seyfeddin and Esma Sultan.</data>
      <data key="d3">8855ef7c0a862ad2716a4800e6daab9a4fc8a3fc3144bf260d69fbc7114ab5f6_chunk_0&lt;SEP&gt;00abc8939d8e5e0dd3acda099aa550f155b8386dfee901c16f211d045eb300dc_chunk_0</data>
      <data key="d4">null</data>
    </node>
    <node id="abd lmecid ii">
      <data key="d0">abd lmecid ii</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Abdülmecid II was the last Caliph of the Muslim world and the half-brother of Esma Sultan, representing a significant figure in the Ottoman dynasty.</data>
      <data key="d3">8855ef7c0a862ad2716a4800e6daab9a4fc8a3fc3144bf260d69fbc7114ab5f6_chunk_0</data>
      <data key="d4">null</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ottoman empire">
      <data key="d0">ottoman empire</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Ottoman Empire was a historical empire that existed from the late 13th century until the early 20th century, known for its vast territory and significant influence in the region.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ottoman Empire was a historical empire that spanned across Europe, Asia, and Africa, known for its significant influence on the regions it governed, particularly during the reigns of its sultans.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ottoman Empire was a historical empire that spanned across Europe, Asia, and Africa, known for its significant political and military influence, particularly during the time of Küçük Hüseyin Pasha.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ottoman Empire was a historical empire that ruled over a vast territory, including the region where the Laleli Mosque is located, influencing its architecture and culture.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ottoman Empire was a historical empire that existed from 1299 to 1922, known for its vast territorial expanse and significant cultural contributions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ottoman Empire was a significant historical empire that existed from the late 13th century until the early 20th century, known for its vast territorial expanse and cultural influence.</data>
      <data key="d3">8855ef7c0a862ad2716a4800e6daab9a4fc8a3fc3144bf260d69fbc7114ab5f6_chunk_0&lt;SEP&gt;ab86467d215b61cd3bcb04f178aad33bd273548437a1beb351bd76fe7575dae8_chunk_0&lt;SEP&gt;d7732993584e6052219909b3713bcfd07c3e2fe072a2d0dc3208947e7a9939a3_chunk_0&lt;SEP&gt;4e34fde3d478bc36a644cfb15e082fe3571707a1e0045af76e8cc63b738160af_chunk_0&lt;SEP&gt;00abc8939d8e5e0dd3acda099aa550f155b8386dfee901c16f211d045eb300dc_chunk_0&lt;SEP&gt;aabfddd60fb33fe357ce8061fbadd36dd9b83032d9ea1817dc5bd725a9512e25_chunk_0</data>
